was led by the Belarussian, " [:a {:href "/athletes/96205"} "Aleksey Parfenkov"] ". But Parfenkov finished last on both jumps in the final, placing last of the finalists. Schönbächler’s first final jump was a back full-full-full (bFFF), and he placed first, narrowly leading two Canadians, " [:a {:href "/athletes/89407"} "Lloyd Langlois"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/89433"} "Philippe LaRoche"] " (the current World Cup leader). In the second round, Schönbächler again placed first, this time with a back full-double full-full (bFdFF), to secure the gold medal. LaRoche placed second in the second round and moved up to the silver medal. Langlois struggled, placing only 7th in the second jump, but hung on for the bronze medal. LaRoche had won the aerials event in 1992 at Albertville when it was a demonstration event, while Langlois had placed third."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/97377"} "Sonny Schönbächler"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "196.53 (10)"] [:td {} "234.67 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/89433"} "Philippe LaRoche"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "222.65 (2)"] [:td {} "228.63 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/89407"} "Lloyd La